libc: the EmiBSD target in the crate std links

Why a patch: the libc crate std links (0.2.185, what the release's
library/Cargo.lock fixes) selects its bindings by target_os, and EmiBSD's
libc presents the same interface as OpenBSD's (D-0003): `target_os =
"emibsd"` joins every condition that names "openbsd" in the crate's module
selection (unix, bsd, netbsdlike, new), and its build script allows the
value for check-cfg; the OpenBSD module asks for libexecinfo, which EmiBSD
does not have, so not for emibsd. The crate comes from its EmiBSD mirror as .emibsd/libc
(UPSTREAM.toml); rust/build/build.sh puts it, patched, in the place of the
vendored libc-0.2.185, a vendored package with no checksum, so cargo builds
it as the registry crate it replaces, with the same lint cap; library/
Cargo.lock therefore drops the registry checksum of libc 0.2.185: the crate
is no longer the registry's. Written by EmiBSD (ISC); carried by DevTools
over the pinned tags, offered upstream when stable. Author: Emilio
Navarrete Lineros, 2026-10-31.

